# Rocketship layout

Reasons: `_planning/component-review-decisions.md`.

## Viewport media queries

- Use `@include media-breakpoint-up(md)` only in Container and layout code, and in `variables.scss` for `:root` spacing. Never in a component.
- Breakpoints are min-width, mobile-first and in px: `$rs-breakpoints` in `styles/mixins/breakpoints.scss`. Never redeclare them.

## Container queries

- Only for a layout change: a Grid gaining columns, Card media moving beside the text. Never for size, type or density steps.
- A component with one layout has one size. Body copy never shrinks.
- Write `@include container-query-up($rs-cq-md)`. Thresholds `$rs-cq-sm/md/lg` (500/700/900px) live in `styles/mixins/container-query.scss`.
- It queries the nearest container of any kind. Put `container-type: inline-size` on layout boxes (pages, panels), never on a leaf component.
- Never tie a component's size to the viewport.

## Container component

- `.rs-container` sets max-width and page gutters (`--rs-container-gutter`, `-left`, `-right`).
- Widths: default (`--rs-container-width-default`, no modifier), `wide` (1200px), `content` (600px, 800px at `lg`), `full`.
- `padded` adds vertical inset from `--rs-container-padding-block` (20/30/40px at base/`md`/`lg`, set on `:root` in `variables.scss`). Unpadded containers set it to `0`.
- `--rs-container-padding-block-start` / `-end` override one side. They resolve with the safe area into `--rs-container-gutter-top` / `-bottom`.

## Scrolling

- Scrolling belongs to whoever places the content. Wrap it in `<Scroll>`; components never scroll themselves.
- `<Scroll>` scrolls sideways when content is too wide. `vertical` adds up-and-down scrolling, capped by `--rs-scroll-max-block-size` (default `70dvh`).
